    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pleasanton was founded in 1854 on rolling prairie that drew early farmers and livestock raisers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasanton_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as Pleasant Plain, named for its grassy landscape, with the first lot sold July 5, 1854, and the plat filed September 28, 1855.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasanton_iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1883 a narrow-gauge railroad was brought in after residents raised $10,000, briefly prompting a name change to 'Harding' before reverting to Pleasanton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasanton_iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pleasanton's economy has remained anchored in farming and stock raising since the late 19th century, with limited diversification beyond its local trading hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
